{{fbdoc item="title" value="BASSMOD"}}----
BASSMOD is a MOD only (XM, IT, S3M, MOD, MTM, UMX) version of BASS - useful for demos, or anything else where you want to play some MOD music.

Website: https://www.un4seen.com/bassmod.html
Platforms supported: ""Win32"", Linux i386
Headers to include: bassmod.bi
Header version: 2.0, with opt-in 2.1 attribute declarations
Examples: in examples/sound/BASS/

{{fbdoc item="section" value="SDK and target selection"}}
	BASSMOD is a separate legacy library, not the current BASS 2.4 SDK. The Windows 2.0 DLL and the author's Linux 2.1 hotfix are 32-bit i386 libraries. On a 64-bit PC, build a 32-bit executable and provide the matching FreeBASIC runtime and library. A 64-bit executable cannot link or load these binaries.

	The Windows SDK is available at https://www.un4seen.com/files/bassmod20.zip. The Linux hotfix is available at https://www.un4seen.com/stuff/bassmod-linux.zip, as linked by the author at https://www.un4seen.com/forum/?topic=12858.0. Keep each SDK's headers and binary together.

	The header defaults to the original 2.0 API. When using the Linux 2.1 hotfix's attribute API, define ##BASSMOD_21## before including ##bassmod.bi##. That selects ##BASSMOD_MusicSetAttribute## and ##BASSMOD_MusicGetAttribute## in place of the old amplify, pan separation, position scaler and channel/instrument volume functions removed in 2.1. Common playback and decoding calls used below work with both versions.

	##DWORD## and ##HSYNC## are always 32-bit vendor values, including on Unix. ##BASSMOD_GetVersion## places the major version in the low 16 bits and the minor version in the high 16 bits: 2.0 returns 2 and 2.1 returns 65538.

{{fbdoc item="section" value="Playback and errors"}}
	The Linux library uses the legacy OSS device interface. It requires a working ##/dev/dsp## character device, supplied by an OSS driver or a compatible driver such as osspd with an ALSA backend. The library checks device existence before opening it, so an ALSA preload wrapper alone cannot initialize playback when that device is absent.

	Device -1 requests default output. Device -2 disables sound output, and device -3 selects decoding only. Successful initialization with either negative special device does not demonstrate output-device support.

	The example accepts a module filename as its first command-line argument. With no argument it uses the bundled module relative to the executable's normal example directory. Set ##FB_EXAMPLE_AUTOPLAY=1## for a bounded playback check without keyboard input. Initialization, loading, starting and stopping failures return a nonzero exit status; the library's void cleanup procedures are called before exit.

{{fbdoc item="ex"}}
{{fbdoc item="filename" value="examples/manual/libraries/bassmod.bas"}}%%(freebasic)
'' examples/manual/libraries/bassmod.bas
''
'' Example extracted from the FreeBASIC Manual
'' from topic 'BASSMOD'
'' Purpose: Play a module with the native BASSMOD 2.x library.
'' Responsibilities: File selection, playback errors and library cleanup.
'' This example contains no module decoder or output driver implementation.
''
'' See Also: https://www.freebasic.net/wiki/wikka.php?wakka=ExtLibbassmod
'' --------

#include Once "bassmod.bi"

Dim As String sound_file = Command(1)
If sound_file = "" Then sound_file = ExePath() & "/../../sound/data/dne_trtn.mod"

If ((BASSMOD_GetVersion() And &hffff) <> 2) Then
	Print "BASSMOD version 2 required!"
	End 1
End If

If (BASSMOD_Init(-1, 44100, 0) = 0) Then
	Print "Could not initialize BASSMOD: "; BASSMOD_ErrorGetCode()
	End 1
End If

If (BASSMOD_MusicLoad(False, StrPtr(sound_file), 0, 0, BASS_MUSIC_LOOP) = 0) Then
	Print "BASSMOD could not load '" & sound_file & "'"
	BASSMOD_Free()
	End 1
End If

If BASSMOD_MusicPlay() = 0 Then
	Print "Could not start playback: "; BASSMOD_ErrorGetCode()
	BASSMOD_MusicFree()
	BASSMOD_Free()
	End 1
End If

Dim As Integer playback_error = 0
If Environ("FB_EXAMPLE_AUTOPLAY") = "1" Then
	'' Wait for actual module progress without requiring keyboard input.
	Sleep 1200, 1
	Dim As DWORD position = BASSMOD_MusicGetPosition()
	If BASSMOD_MusicIsActive() <> BASS_ACTIVE_PLAYING OrElse _
		position = 0 OrElse position = Cast(DWORD, -1) Then playback_error = 1
Else
	Print "Sound playing; waiting for keypress to stop and exit..."
	Sleep
End If

If BASSMOD_MusicStop() = 0 Then playback_error = 1
BASSMOD_MusicFree()
BASSMOD_Free()
If playback_error Then End 1
Print "BASSMOD playback completed."

'' end of bassmod.bas
%%

